                <pb facs="0344" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg334"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-11-02T17:00:00+08:00">November 2, 1948—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 2—8:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2065. Admiral Badger is preparing cable CNO regarding action contemplated under
                    revised directive Deptel 1505, October 27<anchor n="50" xml:id="d278-f1"/> which
                    closely parallels third alternative our 1871, October 8, 3 p.m. He is urging
                    dependents depart but feels repercussions locally from ordered evacuation
                    dependents would have harmful effect outweighing beneficial evacuation all
                    dependents. He expressed to Minister-Counselor complete confidence his ability
                    evacuate on short notice Navy dependents as well as all Americans Tsingtao
                    without in any way affecting his ability handle any emergency evacuation
                    situation arising North China.</p>
                <p>Danger point [would be?] should Communists fail to heed his protestations of
                    neutrality, demand his immediate evacuation and endeavor overrun his
                    installations. Under such circumstances Badger, quite rightly we believe,
                    refuses to commit himself in advance as to action he would take. Such action, he
                    says, would depend on circumstances.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
